+            <div class="row"><div class="k">Stop rules</div><div class="v">Final answer, user cancellation, MCP timeout or terminal refusal, context exhaustion, identity mismatch, malformed high-level proposal, or a request for an unsupported visual route. There is no arbitrary task-call cutoff. One Agent Mode inference stops as no progress after 2,048 consecutive generated tokens produce neither visible answer text nor a completed tool call; this conservative POC threshold allows a normal short proposal while preventing a hidden turn from consuming the remaining 64K context, and no new MCP request is dispatched from that stalled step. The same local proposal rejected three times on unchanged canonical sanitized screen content stops with its exact validation reason, even when other rejected proposals or read-only observations occur between attempts. A meaningfully changed screen or successful submitted operation clears that tracker. When no stable screen identity exists, the original three-consecutive-identical rule remains. At most 24 distinct rejection signatures are retained for one stable screen. Successful high-level <code>observe</code> choices have a separate bounded no-progress guard: the host retains only one SHA-256 digest and count for the canonical sanitized result. A changed result or successful dispatched mutation resets it. The third equivalent read returns one explicit correction to use a current action or editable-field selector, finish, or report a blocker. A fourth equivalent read after that correction ends the attempt with a precise read-only no-progress reason. This does not count internal recovery reads and is not a total tool or MCP-call limit. Three equivalent recoverable <code>CACHE_COLD_MISS</code> results for the same normalized host request also stop as no progress. A first or second cold miss with explicit <code>dispatch_attempted=false</code> remains recoverable, but the refused action is never replayed automatically. <code>GUARDED_TAR