+            <div class="row"><div class="k">Runtime configuration</div><div class="v">64K context, 32 expert-cache slots, temperature 0.20, Top-K 64, Top-P 0.95, Prefill on, and RDADVISE off.</div></div>
+            <div class="row"><div class="k">Journey evidence</div><div class="v">All six onboarding steps completed. Each of the two native alerts followed <code>describe system alert</code> &rarr; one exact <code>Allow</code> press carrying the returned digest &rarr; one read-only <code>describe system alert</code>. No pointer request was used. The run reached Add Profile, submitted Done, then stopped after the second stale refusal for the same unchanged-screen action. The terminal context reading was 4.6K of 66K with 32 tool calls.</div></div>
+            <div class="row"><div class="k">Memory evidence</div><div class="v"><code>/tmp/turbo-alert-cycle-retest-memory.csv</code> contains 63 samples. Combined process memory peaked at 2,409,872 KB and averaged 1,117,349 KB. The app peak was 155,632 KB and the decode-service peak was 2,319,856 KB.</div></div>
+            <div class="row"><div class="k">Remaining blocker</div><div class="v">The proof cannot claim full-app exploration until VisionCapture resolves the repeat <code>CACHE_ACTION_CAPABILITY_STALE</code> cache-binding failure on an unchanged screen. No additional source change, rebuild, deployment, unit test, live run, commit, or push was performed while recording this verification.</div></div>
+            <div class="row"><div class="k">Later ordered-run finding</div><div class="v">A later clean ordered run completed onboarding and both alert routes, then stopped after Gemma proposed the same named type target three times. One misspelled tool name was correctly returned as <code>Not sent</code>. The repeated target was also never sent. The failure was in the adapter: VisionCapture&rsquo;s <code>describe screen</code> result publishes visible editable elements in structured <code>elements</code> with exact labels and identifiers, while TurboFieldfare discarded those fields and incorrectly checked typing against the cache action list used for taps and switches. Observing again therefore could not provide a valid type target. The run ended at 4,942 total tokens and 39 tool calls. <code>/tmp/turbo-ordered-nestmind-memory.csv</code> contains 62 samples: combined peak 2,034,640 KB, combined average 1,224,680 KB, app peak 172,320 KB, and service peak 1,938,256 KB.</div></div>
